<title>ISRAEL: Elbit Q2 loss/shr $0.09.</title>
<headline>Elbit Q2 loss/shr $0.09.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Elbit Ltd.</p>
<p>		    (in thousands of dollars except loss per share)</p>
<p>				  Q2 97    Q2 96    6-MTH 97   6-MTH 96</p>
<p>Sales			   9,523    9,036    18,855     16,186</p>
<p>Operating Profit (loss)  (2,109)  (1,604)   (3,888)    (2,925)</p>
<p>Net Profit (loss)	  (2,004)  (4,151)   (3,434)    (5,998)</p>
<p>Loss per share		(0.09)   (0.19)    (0.16)     (0.28)</p>
<p>Elbit said the results reflect the transition in the communication field, whose activities are in their early stages.</p>
<p>&quot;The investment in Hynex and CableTel have not yet produced results and a considerable portion of the half-year loss is related to the costs of their development teams,&quot; the Israeli company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Elbit owns 60 percent of Hynex Ltd, which is engaged in data transfer across LANs and WANs. It owns 100 percent of CableTel.</p>
<p>-Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 TCC</p>
</text>
